For the reasoning question, the dependents' claim is the most concrete and pressing—a seasonal society's moral imagination is fundamentally about the people who depend on shared structures through the year. The point about nature (B) is also deeply weighted because such a society reads nature constantly and trusts it as a teacher. The position-based view (A) is foundational but, on its own, incomplete—it needs to be tempered by the other considerations.

